{"id":"d3df486b-89d8-4aa8-97a9-3cad360f4307","object":"chat.completion","created":1785029107,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\":\"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dict\\\")\\n    if \\\"threshold\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"missing threshold\\\")\\n    if \\\"calls\\\" not in case or not isinstance(case[\\\"calls\\\"], list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"missing or invalid calls\\\")\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"threshold must be a number\\\")\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    for item in calls:\\n        if not isinstance(item, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"call item must be dict\\\")\\n        for key in (\\\"call_id\\\", \\\"loss_without_call\\\", \\\"loss_with_call\\\", \\\"prediction_tokens\\\", \\\"parseable\\\"):\\n            if key not in item:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"missing {key} in call\\\")\\n        call_id = item[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        if not isinstance(call_id, str):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"call_id must be string\\\")\\n        loss_without = item[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = item[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)) or not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"loss values must be numbers\\\")\\n        pred_tokens = item[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        if not isinstance(pred_tokens, int) or pred_tokens <= 0:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"prediction_tokens must be positive integer\\\")\\n        parseable = item[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"parseable must be boolean\\\")\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / pred_tokens\\n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain\\n        })\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to write Python code for solve(case) that implements the described task. The task: \"Retain API-call candidates using normalized future-token weights, weighted losses, the stronger counterfactual, and an inclusive threshold.\" \n\nWe have fixture payloads showing: threshold (number), calls (list of objects with call_id, loss_without_call, loss_with_call, prediction_tokens, parseable). \n\nObjective: For each call, compute gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call. Then normalize gain by prediction_tokens? The phrase \"Normalize gain by at least one prediction token.\" and \"normalized_gain\" appears in output schema as a number. So normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens? But \"by at least one prediction token\" might mean divide by max(prediction_tokens, 1)? However prediction_tokens are positive integers in fixtures (2-6). So just divide by prediction_tokens.\n\nThen \"Require both parseability and normalized gain at or above threshold.\" So accepted if parseable is True and normalized_gain >= threshold. Inclusive threshold means >=.\n\n\"Keep diagnostics in supplied call order.\" Output diagnostics array should be in same order as input calls list.\n\n\"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" What rounding? The output schema has normalized_gain as number, but likely we should round to some precision? Not specified but typical: maybe keep as float. But \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" suggests rounding normalized_gain. Could round to something like 8 decimal places? Or maybe to a fixed number? The fixture examples didn't show expected output. However we can just return the computed value. The output schema says type number, no constraints on rounding. To be safe, we can keep as float. But \"rounded\" might be a hint to round to avoid floating point artifacts. Perhaps round to some reasonable precision like 8 decimals. But not required. Since it's not explicitly specified, I'll compute exactly.\n\n\"Use only quantities present in the case payload.\" So no external data.\n\n\"Treat these registered properties as hard contracts: normalized_weights, stronger_counterfactual, inclusive_threshold, stable_order.\" The payload has \"threshold\". \"normalized_weights\" might refer to dividing by prediction_tokens. \"stronger_counterfactual\": maybe the stronger counterfactual is the loss_without_call? Actually loss without call is the baseline. So gain is the reduction. That's the counterfactual. \"inclusive_threshold\": inclusive means >=. \"stable_order\": keep order.\n\n\"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case.\" We need to validate required fields: threshold, calls list, each call has call_id, loss_without_call, loss_with_call, prediction_tokens, parseable. If missing, raise ValueError.\n\nReturn object with accepted_call_ids (list of strings) and diagnostics (list of objects with accepted, call_id, normalized_gain). The diagnostics should include all calls, not only accepted.\n\nImplementation steps:\n1. Validate case structure.\n2. For each call in calls list:\n   - compute gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call\n   - normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\n   - accepted = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\n   - store diagnostics dict.\n3. Build accepted_call_ids list from those with accepted true.\n4. Return dict.\n\nRounding: The instructions say \"rounded per-call diagnostics\". Could round normalized_gain to say 10 decimal places? But fixtures have many decimals. To be safe, I'll return the raw float. But if they expect rounding, we can round to, say, 8 digits. The fixture outputs not given. I'll assume no rounding required; just compute.\n\nWrite code accordingly.\n\nNow produce JSON with key \"implementation\" and value as a string containing Python source. Ensure proper escaping.\n\nLet me write the code:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    # Validate case structure\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"case must be a dict\")\n    if \"threshold\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"missing threshold\")\n    if \"calls\" not in case or not isinstance(case[\"calls\"], list):\n        raise ValueError(\"missing or invalid calls\")\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(\"threshold must be a number\")\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    for item in calls:\n        if not isinstance(item, dict):\n            raise ValueError(\"call item must be dict\")\n        for key in (\"call_id\", \"loss_without_call\", \"loss_with_call\", \"prediction_tokens\", \"parseable\"):\n            if key not in item:\n                raise ValueError(f\"missing {key} in call\")\n        call_id = item[\"call_id\"]\n        if not isinstance(call_id, str):\n            raise ValueError(\"call_id must be string\")\n        loss_without = item[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = item[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)) or not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(\"loss values must be numbers\")\n        pred_tokens = item[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        if not isinstance(pred_tokens, int) or pred_tokens <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"prediction_tokens must be positive integer\")\n        parseable = item[\"parseable\"]\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\n            raise ValueError(\"parseable must be boolean\")\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / pred_tokens\n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"accepted\": accepted,\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain\n        })\n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThat's it. Now escape for JSON.\n\nMake sure no extra whitespace. The response must be exactly one JSON object with key \"implementation\". The value is a JSON string of the Python source.\n\nLet's produce the final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2164,"completion_tokens":1863,"total_tokens":4027,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1312},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":116},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}